+# Design direction
+
+## Frame
+
+A 1920×1080 editorial career map uses generous safe margins, a persistent top-left lesson label, and a slim bottom progress rail. Each beat centers one idea rather than showing the full framework at once.
+
+## Palette and type
+
+Use the supplied SCLA tokens: deep navy grounds, white and cultured-paper cards, blue for structure, and gold only for the active route and decisive proof. Proxima Nova is the display and body face with the provided system fallback. Body copy never falls below 40px; small labels use the allowed 20px floor.
+
+## Visual language
+
+Rounded evidence cards, route nodes, role chips, and concise transformation examples make abstract repositioning concrete. Alex, Jordan, and Priya each receive a distinct initial badge but remain within one system. The gold through-line persists as the unifying metaphor.
+
+## Motion
+
+A single paused, seekable GSAP timeline drives all animation. Each clip enters within 1.2 seconds with a short stagger, holds for reading, and exits before the next beat. Movement is directional and finite: cards rise, proof chips slide forward, and the route draws left-to-right. No infinite motion is used.
